-- R06 — PBOC fix: read the day-on-day change in the fix-minus-estimate gap, not its level.
-- Owner request, 15 Oct 2026 (project thread "PBOC fix gap rule for digests").
-- Proposed 15 Oct 2026 06:02Z from a cloud thread with this exact statement (dash.propose_rule raised
-- no approval prompt); apply_after = Sun 18 Oct 2026 20:00 SGT, when the Sunday "apply rules" task puts
-- it in force unless the owner replies "oppose R06" to the weekly review email. Both digests read it
-- through dash.rules_in_force() at the start of every run. Rerunning this file would propose a new
-- rule id, so run it only to re-propose after a revert.
-- To put it in force before the Sunday window (one line in the Supabase SQL editor):
--   update dash.rules set status = 'in_force', decided_at = now(), apply_after = now() where rid = 'R06' and status = 'proposed';
-- Data the rule relies on: msd.observations, series FX_USDCNH.CFETS_FIX (official CFETS parity, daily,
-- loaded about 05:20 SGT); the estimate is the Reuters survey figure found on the web (the in-house
-- series FX_USDCNH.FIX_MODEL holds no rows as of 15 Oct 2026).
select dash.propose_rule($j${"scope": "both", "title": "PBOC fix: read the day-on-day change in the fix-minus-estimate gap, not its level", "body": "PBOC FIX: READ THE CHANGE IN THE GAP, NOT ITS LEVEL (owner, 15 Oct 2026). The 09:15 SGT USD/CNY fix is set weaker (higher) than the market's model estimate almost every day, so \"weaker than model\" on its own is not a signal and is never written as a bearish-CNY read. The signal is the DAY-ON-DAY CHANGE in the gap: a gap that NARROWS (today's fix closer to its estimate than yesterday's was to its own) is CNY-POSITIVE, the PBOC leaning less against the yuan; a gap that WIDENS is CNY-NEGATIVE.\n\n1. DATA, at the evidence step. The latest fix is the previous session's (today's prints after this run). Fixes: `select as_of, value from msd.observations where series_id = 'FX_USDCNH.CFETS_FIX' and as_of >= current_date - 10 order by as_of;` (official CFETS parity, loaded about 05:20 SGT), or the FXStreet headline \"PBOC sets USD/CNY reference rate at X vs Y previous\". Estimates: the Reuters survey estimate for each session, as quoted by Reuters, FXStreet or the scanners (Bloomberg's survey when Reuters is missing; say which); Reuters' daily yuan report usually states the gap itself (\"N pips weaker than the Reuters estimate of X\"), so take that as given for the session it describes. When sources disagree by more than 30 pips, take Reuters and note the other. If the previous session's estimate cannot be found after one search, print \"prior estimate n/a\" and give no change-based signal that day.\n2. ARITHMETIC. gap = (fix - estimate) x 10,000, in pips, + = weaker than model. change = latest gap - previous gap (- = narrowing). Where the previous sessions' estimates are at hand, list the last 5 gaps.\n3. ONE LINE, wherever the fix is cited and always in the China/CNY theme: \"PBOC fix <date>: <fix> vs est <estimate> = +<gap> pips | prior +<gap> | change <+/-n> | 5-session: <gaps or n/a> | signal: <CNY-positive narrowing / CNY-negative widening / unchanged lean>\". Signal bands: |change| under 50 pips = unchanged lean (the level is context only); 50 pips or more = the signal; 150 pips or more = strong, so name the likely cause (basket move, policy news) in the same sentence. A run of gaps rising over the week = the PBOC leaning harder (CNY-negative); falling = easing its lean (CNY-positive). If today's estimate is already published before the run, add the watch level for 09:15: a fix more than 50 pips above (estimate + prior gap) widens, more than 50 below narrows.\n4. USE. The change-based signal, not the level, is what enters the CNY/CNH theme, the odds-engine questions on CNY, the scanner reconciliation (a scanner that reads the level as bearish is corrected), and every USDCNH, CNY-cross or Asia-FX trade card's catalyst and \"priced\" tests: a weak-side level alone is never the reason to card, size or reject a CNY trade. Keep the dollar's overnight move apart: a fix that is higher only because the basket moved is not a lean.", "rationale": "Owner, 15 Oct 2026: the fix is set weaker than the model estimate nearly every day, so the level carries no information; desks gauge the PBOC's signalling by whether the fix is more or less weak than yesterday relative to the model. The digests had been reading three days of 300-plus-pip gaps as a continuing bearish-CNY lean.", "evidence": "Fable digests 10, 14 and 15 Oct 2026: 'PBOC fixes weaker than models' used as the reason not to card short USDCNH, and 'a second/third day 300-plus pips weak-side' read as pressure, while the gap went from about +317 to +327 pips (unchanged lean under this rule). CFETS fix series FX_USDCNH.CFETS_FIX is in the database daily; the in-house estimate series FX_USDCNH.FIX_MODEL is empty, so the estimate comes from the Reuters survey.", "revert_if": "Revert if a weekly review finds the fix line mis-computed (wrong sign, wrong session or arithmetic) in 2 or more digests, or the estimate unavailable on 3 or more runs in a week.", "supersedes": null, "review_due": "2026-11-23", "source": "owner"}$j$::jsonb);
